===Unsuccessful candidacies===
[[File:Eleições presidenciais 2011.png|thumb|300px|Official logo of the election.]]
*[[Luís Botelho Ribeiro]] – Leader of the [[Portugal Pro-life|Pro-life]] party. His application was formalised on Monday, 20 December, with over 8,000 signatures. His candidacy was analysed by the Constitutional Court. On 29 December, the court concluded that his candidacy did not meet the requirements provided by law.<ref>{{cite news |date=3 January 2011 |url=https://www.dn.pt/dossiers/politica/presidenciais-2011/noticias/tribunal-rejeita-recurso-de-luis-botelho-ribeiro-1747857.html|title=Tribunal rejeita recurso de Luís Botelho Ribeiro |language=pt |work=Diário de Notícias|access-date=12 May 2020}}</ref>
*[[José Ribeiro e Castro]] – Member of the [[Democratic and Social Centre – People´s Party]], speculated to run as an alternative right-wing candidate, because of Cavaco's decision to approve same-sex marriage. However, he did not go forward with his candidacy.<ref>{{cite news |date=9 October 2010 |url=https://expresso.pt/dossies/dossiest_actualidade/dossie_presidenciais_2011/presidenciais-ribeiro-e-castro-nao-apresenta-candidatura=f608176|title=Presidenciais: Ribeiro e Castro não apresenta candidatura |language=pt |work=Expresso|access-date=12 May 2020}}</ref>
*[[José Pinto Coelho]] – Leader of the far-right [[National Renovator Party]]. He declared that his candidacy for the presidency was "cut short" by failing to gather the 7,500 signatures required. He claimed to have gathered 5,878 signatures.<ref>{{cite news |date=22 December 2010 |url=https://tvi24.iol.pt/politica/pinto-coelho/lider-do-pnr-desiste-da-candidatura-a-belem|title=Líder do PNR desiste da candidatura a Belém |language=pt |work=TVI24|access-date=12 May 2020}}</ref>

==Campaign period==
===Issues===
The country's deep economic crisis and the [[Banco Português de Negócios|Portuguese Bank of Business]] (BPN) case dominated the campaign. On this latter issue, the nationalization of the bank, linked to figures from the ''Cavacoism'' era, created an embarrassment for the incumbent President, with his opponents questioning his silence and relationship with those involved in the bank's collapse.<ref name="rtp">{{cite news |url=https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/politica/cavaco-bateu-soares-e-tropecou-na-crise-no-caso-bpn_n1706494 |title=Cavaco bateu Soares e "tropeçou" na crise no caso BPN |language=pt |work=RTP|access-date=9 July 2026 |date=29 December 2025}}</ref> Cavaco accused his adversaries of "vile baseness" and of spreading lies and insinuations.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/politica/cavaco-silva-diz-se-alvo-de-uma-campanha-de-vil-baixeza_v407558 |title=Cavaco Silva diz-se alvo de uma campanha de "vil baixeza" |language=pt |work=RTP|access-date=9 July 2026 |date=16 January 2011}}</ref> On the left-wing, Manuel Alegre repeated his 2006 run, but this time with the official support from the PS and the [[Left Bloc]]. However, his candidacy created divisions within the Socialists,<ref>{{cite news |url=https://arquivos.rtp.pt/conteudos/manuel-alegre-e-as-presidenciais/ |title=Manuel Alegre e as presidenciais |language=pt |work=RTP|access-date=9 July 2026 |date=19 January 2010}}</ref> with some supporting the independent candidacy of [[Fernando Nobre]],<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.publico.pt/2010/04/14/politica/noticia/militantes-socialistas-de-santarem-com-a-candidatura-de-fernando-nobre-1432213 |title=Militantes socialistas de Santarém com a candidatura de Fernando Nobre |language=pt |work=Público|access-date=9 July 2026 |date=14 April 2010}}</ref> including the [[Maria Barroso|wife]] and daughter of former president [[Mário Soares]],<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.publico.pt/2010/10/29/politica/noticia/mulher-e-filha-de-mario-soares-apoiam-campanha-de-fernando-nobre-1463486 |title=Mulher e filha de Mário Soares apoiam campanha de Fernando Nobre  |language=pt |work=Público|access-date=9 July 2026 |date=29 October 2010}}</ref> while Soares himself criticized the PS support for Alegre and refused to endorse him.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://arquivos.rtp.pt/conteudos/soares-e-o-apoio-a-alegre/ |title=Soares e o apoio a Alegre |language=pt |work=RTP|access-date=9 July 2026 |date=1 June 2010}}</ref>

